-- title:
--   Functions regular off the ends lift to disc-regular integral functions, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` denotes its residue field. A finset $W$ of places of the characteristic-free modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries κ` generated by the two $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) is assumed, by `hW`, to have as its members exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and have $w(\,$`jGeomGen κ M'`$\,)$ in `ssJSet q κ`; a member $s$ of $W$ is fixed. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; `P.ord` is the associated normalised additive valuation and `P.evalAt f` is the value of $f$ at $P$, defined via the residue map and a section of $K \to$ `P.ResidueField`.
--
--   The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of intermediate fields of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the first being the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$, the second the base change of the function field of the $H$-level curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with the constants is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with $A$ on constants, a scaling property, and a degree- and order-preserving map on places), and `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and has $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   On the reduction side, $FSS$ is a field and a $\kappa$-algebra, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ meeting the constants in $A$, with surjective residue map onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, and satisfying the scaling property), $N$ is a finset of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, and for every place $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ there are given a subring $S_Q =$ `Sx Q` of `fieldBar q M'`, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A[X] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$, and a set $D_Q =$ `Dx Q` of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are as follows. `h0`: $FSS$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$. `h1`: for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order, if the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle` is $R$-integral and its $R$-residue is the image in $FSS$ of $s(\,R_0$-residue of $f)$ under `algebraMap κ FSS`. `h2`: for every $\zeta :$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is preserved by the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`. `hcard`: $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` (fourteen clauses, summarised here) requires, for every $Q \notin N$: that $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$; that $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; that $\varphi_Q$ is the identity on constants from $A$ and that $\chi_{0,Q} \circ \varphi_Q$ is the residue map of $A$ on constants, with $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X)) = 0$; that for every $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ there is a unique $A$-point $\chi : S_Q \to A$ fixing the constants, reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ and sending $\varphi_Q(X)$ to $c$; that every element of $S_Q$ is $R$-integral with $R$-residue in the valuation subring of $Q$, whose residue at $Q$ is the image of its $\chi_{0,Q}$-value; that the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q(X)$ has order $1$ at $Q$; that $D_Q$ consists exactly of the rational places $P$ at which every element of $S_Q$ is regular with value in $A$, and at which the value of $f \in S_Q$ has valuation $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f) = 0$; that every $A$-point of $S_Q$ over the constants reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ is realised by a unique place of $D_Q$; that for $P \in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_Q$ and $h(P) \neq 0$; that a nonzero element of `fieldBar q M'` with order $0$ at all places of $D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant; and that an $R$-integral element regular at all places of $D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, the discs $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ are disjoint unless $Q = Q'$. `hcusp`: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $q$-expansion `jq` has non-negative order at $P$. `heqv`: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the level automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta :$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism `R.resAut τ` preserves membership in $N$, and for $Q \notin N$ it carries the disc $D_Q$ to $D_{(\mathrm{R.resAut}\,\tau) \cdot Q}$, in the sense that `smulDisc τ (Dx Q) = Dx (R.resAut τ hτ • Q)`.
--
--   `hUniq`: for $Q \notin N$, any quadruple $(S, \varphi, \chi_0, D)$ satisfying the same fourteen clauses as above satisfies $D = D_Q$, $S = S_Q$, and $\chi_0$ agrees with $\chi_{0,Q}$ on their common domain.
--
--   `hdl`: for every $\kappa$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ over `GaloisField q 2`, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain and every $\zeta :$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $FSS$ onto the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) inside the Drinfeld function field, such that the cardinality of $C_s$ equals $2 \cdot$ `placeWidthChar q M' s` (with `placeWidthChar` the quotient of `jWidthChar q` at the $j$-value of $s$ by `placeRamificationJ M' s`), and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\,$`redQ q γ`$, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the map $e$ intertwines `R.resAut (levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹)` on $FSS$ with the action `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` of that element on the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   `haff`: there exists a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` containing the image of $A$, contained in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, contained in $S_Q$ for every $Q \notin N$, and such that every $z \in FSS$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every $z \in FSS$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$, there exist $g \in$ `fieldBar q M'` and a proof that $g \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ such that the $R$-residue of $g$ is $z$, and such that for every $Q \notin N$ and every $P \in D_Q$ the element $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and its value $P(g)$ lies in $A$.
--
--   This is a step in the analysis of the supersingular component of the special fibre of a modular curve at the prime $q = 3$ at the auxiliary rigid level governed by $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$: every function on that component which is regular away from the $q+1$ ends is shown to lift to a function integral for the regular prolongation $R$ and regular with $A$-integral values on each smooth residue disc. It is used in the construction of explicit generators for the affine chart of the component minus its ends.
